Drag was measured on three nominally smooth circular cylinders towed through a laboratory tank. The cylinders had diameters of 25.4, 38.1, and 50.8 mm and were tested at carriage speeds from 0.2 to 1.1 m s\(^{-1}\), with a nominal submerged length of 0.60 m. A load cell measured the streamwise force; tare-subtracted voltage was converted to force using calibration data from the relevant measurement campaign. Drag coefficients were calculated using the projected area \(DL\), water density of 998 kg m\(^ {-3}\), and temperature-dependent water viscosity for each run. The corrected Reynolds numbers span approximately 4.3\(\times10^3\) to 5.2\(\times10^4\). Run 17 was excluded because its recorded force is inconsistent with the neighboring 2 in. cylinder measurements and the run log flags a possible zero drift. The coefficient-versus-Reynolds-number data are shown in Fig. 1.
